  "output": "## Accessibility audit: Settings\n\nInput: JSX, 8 elements. The script ran 34 of 38 checks and found 6 (4 failure, 2 advisory). This is not a conformance claim: only the checks listed here ran. The four page-level checks were skipped because the input is a fragment.\n\n### Findings\n1. **heading-order** · SC 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (A) · advisory\n   Element: `<h4>` (line 5)\n   Affects: screen reader\n   Problem: The heading level jumps from h2 to h4, so the outline a screen reader user navigates has a hole.\n   Fix (style the size with CSS if needed):\n   ```diff\n   - <h4>Notifications</h4>\n   + <h3>Notifications</h3>\n   ```\n\n2. **label-orphan** · SC 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (A) · failure\n   Element: `<label htmlFor=\"mail\">` (line 6)\n   Affects: screen reader, voice control\n   Problem: The label points to id \"mail\" and no element has that id.\n   Fix:\n   ```diff\n   - <label htmlFor=\"mail\">Email me</label>\n   + <label htmlFor=\"mailbox\">Email me</label>\n   ```\n\n3. **form-label** · SC 3.3.2 Labels or Instructions (A) · failure\n   Element: `<input id=\"mailbox\" type=\"checkbox\" />` (line 7)\n   Affects: screen reader, voice control\n   Problem: The field has no label, so a screen reader announces it with no name and voice control cannot target it.\n   Fix: this is the same change as finding 2. The existing \"Email me\" label becomes this field's label, so you don't need a second label.\n   ```diff\n   - <label htmlFor=\"mail\">Email me</label>\n   + <label htmlFor=\"mailbox\">Email me</label>\n     <input id=\"mailbox\" type=\"checkbox\" />\n   ```\n\n4. **native-element** · SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · advisory\n   Element: `<div role=\"button\" tabIndex={0} onClick={save}>` (line 8)\n   Affects: keyboard, screen reader\n   Problem: `role=\"button\"` on a div rebuilds what `<button>` already does, and it needs extra scripts for keys and states.\n   Fix (a native button is already focusable, so `role` and `tabIndex={0}` go):\n   ```diff\n   - <div role=\"button\" tabIndex={0} onClick={save}>Save</div>\n   + <button type=\"button\" onClick={save}>Save</button>\n   ```\n\n5. **link-no-href** · SC 2.1.1 Keyboard (A) · failure\n   Element: `<a onClick={reset}>` (line 9)\n   Affects: keyboard\n   Problem: The anchor has no href, so it is not in the Tab order and a screen reader does not treat it as a link.\n   Fix (it runs a script, so it should be a button):\n   ```diff\n   - <a onClick={reset}>Reset</a>\n   + <button type=\"button\" onClick={reset}>Reset</button>\n   ```\n\n6. **tabindex-positive** · SC 2.4.3 Focus Order (A) · failure\n   Element: `<input tabIndex={2} aria-label=\"Search\" />` (line 10)\n   Affects: keyboard\n   Problem: `tabIndex={2}` puts this field ahead of the natural order, so Tab jumps around the page.\n   Fix (to change the order, move the element in the markup and use only 0 or -1):\n   ```diff\n   - <input tabIndex={2} aria-label=\"Search\" />\n   + <input aria-label=\"Search\" />\n   ```\n\n### Needs a manual test\n- Keyboard only: press Tab through the whole input. Every control should be reachable, the order should follow the reading order, and focus should never get trapped (SC 2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3).\n- Screen reader (for example NVDA with Firefox, or VoiceOver with Safari): names, roles, states and headings should be spoken as expected (SC 4.1.2, 1.3.1).\n- Voice control (for example Voice Control or Dragon): say each visible label and check that it activates the control (SC 2.5.3).\n- Zoom and reflow: set the browser to 200%, then to 400% at 1280 CSS px wide (about 320 CSS px). No content should be lost and nothing should need scrolling in two directions (SC 1.4.4, 1.4.10).\n- Alt text quality: the script checks that alt text exists; a person must check that it says what the image is for (SC 1.1.1).\n- Forms: submit with errors and check that the screen reader announces each error and moves to the first one (SC 3.3.1, 4.1.3).\n- Page-level checks (language, title, viewport, main landmark) were skipped because the input is a fragment. Run them on the full page.\n\n### Not checked here\n- Contrast, focus-ring style, spacing and target size: not checked; ui-polish owns them.\n- Whether the flow makes sense and whether the words are clear: not part of this audit.\n\n### Open questions\n- None.",
